<%# Cropper.js, for the shared crop-photo modal. Render on a page that can open
    the cropper (an avatar field, a banner editor), so the library (~40 KB)
    loads only where an upload trigger exists.

    The behaviour around it (cropPhotoModal, imageUploadHost,
    submitFormWithProgress) is studio/cropper and studio/image_upload, on every
    page through studio/alpine_scopes; this partial loads the library alone.

    Pair with: the crop-photo and saving modal registrations in your modal-host
    block (see the README and CHANGELOG), and x-data="imageUploadHost({...})".

    SERVED BY THE HOST'S ASSET PIPELINE, since engine-skipped-transition-fix.
    The two files were cdnjs tags, and a cdnjs connection that never answered
    held the page's load event (the deferred script) on every page that renders
    this partial. They are the cropperjs 1.6.2 npm package's dist files, byte for
    byte (app/assets/javascripts/studio/cropper-1.6.2.min.js and
    app/assets/stylesheets/studio/cropper-1.6.2.min.css); bin/cropper-sri-live
    checks them against the npm tarball and cdnjs's published SRI.

    Both tags keep Subresource Integrity, so a changed file fails to load
    rather than running. The hashes are sha384 over the exact files. A version
    bump replaces both files (new names), recomputes both hashes (openssl dgst
    -sha384 -binary FILE | openssl base64 -A) and runs bin/cropper-sri-live. %>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset_path("studio/cropper-1.6.2.min.css") %>"
      integrity="sha384-6LFfkTKLRlzFtgx8xsWyBdKGpcMMQTkv+dB7rAbugeJAu1Ym2q1Aji1cjHBG12Xh"
      crossorigin="anonymous">
<script defer src="<%= asset_path("studio/cropper-1.6.2.min.js") %>"
        integrity="sha384-jrOgQzBlDeUNdmQn3rUt/PZD+pdcRBdWd/HWRqRo+n2OR2QtGyjSaJC0GiCeH+ir"
        crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
